Translation patch: `ParsedNamedParams::parse` (building the query and the parameter names)

Change: The loop `for (colon_offset, start, end) in params { real_query.extend(&query[last..colon_offset]); real_query.push(b'?'); last = end; out_params.push(Cow::Borrowed(&query[start..end])); } real_query.extend(&query[last..]);` becomes a call `substitute_params(query, &params, 0, 0, real_query, out_params)` of a new recursive function that handles `params[k]` the same way and then calls itself on `k + 1` with `last = end`; at `k == params.len()` it appends `&query[last..]` and returns both vectors. `Vec::extend(&[u8])` becomes `Vec::extend_from_slice`.
Why: As an index loop, Aeneas fails with an internal error ("Found an already registered mapping") on pushing `Cow::Borrowed(&query[..])` borrows into a `Vec` inside a loop; a recursion needs no loop fixed point (as in patch 30). `Extend<&T> for Vec<T>` is not modelled by Aeneas (`extend_from_slice` is).
Behaviour: Identical: the same slices are appended and pushed in the same order (`Extend<&T> for Vec<T: Copy>` appends the slice's elements, as `extend_from_slice` does). Stack: the patched copy recurses once per named parameter, where the loop used constant stack (the Lean model does not model the stack).

